1
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:20,369
You had this kid followed?

2
00:00:20,369 --> 00:00:22,666
Are you trying to pick a fight
with the Ferells?

3
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:23,773
What are you talking about?

4
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:25,308
Can you just stop using my daughter

5
00:00:25,308 --> 00:00:27,043
so you won't feel guilty about what happened?

6
00:00:27,043 --> 00:00:29,578
Celestina is alive!

7
00:00:29,578 --> 00:00:32,281
I can feel it in my heart.

8
00:00:32,281 --> 00:00:35,651
And if you refuse to believe that,
let me look for her.

9
00:00:35,651 --> 00:00:37,653
Don't force me to believe
that Celestina is still alive,

10
00:00:37,653 --> 00:00:39,021
because she's already dead.

11
00:00:39,021 --> 00:00:42,058
She and Alyanna are already dead,
and that's what I can feel!

12
00:00:42,058 --> 00:00:44,193
Stop chasing ghosts.

13
00:00:44,193 --> 00:00:48,564
Stop chasing the past
before you get hurt or hurt someone else.

14
00:00:48,564 --> 00:00:51,667
Can I ask a favor from you?

15
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:53,336
Anything.

16
00:00:53,336 --> 00:00:57,873
Would it be okay
if you oversee some things during the ball?

17
00:00:57,873 --> 00:01:00,176
I can only handle the preparations.

18
00:01:00,176 --> 00:01:01,377
You're not coming?

19
00:01:01,377 --> 00:01:04,847
I'm just a scholar here in GU.

20
00:01:04,847 --> 00:01:08,084
I can't afford that 50,000 pesos.

21
00:01:08,084 --> 00:01:11,454
Florence, oh, come on.

22
00:01:11,454 --> 00:01:13,022
You'll be there.

23
00:01:13,022 --> 00:01:16,926
And I'm sure
Nero will ask you to be his date.

24
00:01:16,926 --> 00:01:19,561
He'll pay for you.

25
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:48,975
For you.

26
00:01:55,297 --> 00:01:57,733
I'm happy that you invited me, Sir.

27
00:01:57,733 --> 00:02:01,037
Your sizeable contribution
to our beloved university

28
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:02,438
will certainly be a big help.

29
00:02:02,438 --> 00:02:04,940
Which brings me to my point.

30
00:02:06,742 --> 00:02:08,911
I'm interested in one of your scholars.

31
00:02:08,911 --> 00:02:10,513
Scholars?

32
00:02:10,513 --> 00:02:12,048
Yes.

33
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:15,584
Her name is Florence Dela Cruz.

34
00:02:15,584 --> 00:02:18,888
And if possible,
I would like to know everything about her.

35
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:23,391
Words, if it comes from the heart,
can be comforting.

36
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:27,502
But in our case right now, it won't work.

37
00:02:27,502 --> 00:02:30,800
Because it's more effective
if you cry out all your pain.

38
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,803
Take out all the pain
you're feeling right now.

39
00:02:33,803 --> 00:02:41,803
To be fair, you were able to say words
that made me feel better.

40
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,335
Mama!

41
00:03:39,732 --> 00:03:41,885
Who's there? Is the white van there?

42
00:03:41,885 --> 00:03:45,088
Lord, please no,
I still have a lot of dreams.

43
00:03:51,761 --> 00:03:54,810
Grandfather Garp, what's this for?

44
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:59,682
This is your chance to tell the truth,
or else...

45
00:03:59,682 --> 00:04:03,318
You know we know
where you feel ticklish the most.

46
00:04:06,022 --> 00:04:11,627
- Here, I know you'll get tickled by this.
- Okay, I'll tell the truth!

47
00:04:11,627 --> 00:04:13,996
What really happened?

48
00:04:13,996 --> 00:04:16,766
Grandfather, I'm not a gossip-monger but...

49
00:04:16,766 --> 00:04:19,201
it all started that day...

50
00:04:20,469 --> 00:04:23,472
Florence needed help.

51
00:04:25,875 --> 00:04:27,976
She's my girlfriend.

52
00:04:36,534 --> 00:04:43,742
Supposedly, to save Florence
from the mean girls who are bullying her.

53
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:46,911
But, Nero has a different agenda.

54
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,955
Florence, hi.

55
00:04:56,955 --> 00:04:58,757
Hi, Antonia.

56
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:01,826
Nero. Congratulations to you both.

57
00:05:01,826 --> 00:05:04,528
You guys make such a cute couple.

58
00:05:06,698 --> 00:05:08,533
Thank you.

59
00:05:08,533 --> 00:05:10,802
What happened?

60
00:05:10,802 --> 00:05:13,371
I don't know the details, Grandfather.

61
00:05:13,371 --> 00:05:19,711
I can just imagine
that the pretense slowly became true.

62
00:05:19,711 --> 00:05:23,914
And at the very least,
it was true for Florence.

63
00:05:37,729 --> 00:05:39,164
Really?

64
00:05:39,164 --> 00:05:42,967
Did they spend one night
in each other's arms...

65
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:44,602
under the rain?

66
00:05:44,602 --> 00:05:47,305
I just imagined that, Grandfather.
You're something else.

67
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:49,541
How would I know what the real scene was?

68
00:05:49,541 --> 00:05:53,178
Do I watch them 24/7?

69
00:05:53,178 --> 00:05:55,976
Your imagination is okay, bro...

70
00:05:55,976 --> 00:05:58,249
Just like the movies.

71
00:05:58,249 --> 00:06:03,020
Yes, it's like a rated SPG movie.

72
00:06:03,755 --> 00:06:06,324
Well, what I know is...

73
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:11,629
the make-believe ended up
with them having real feelings,

74
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:15,199
especially for Florence.

75
00:06:16,201 --> 00:06:18,770
That's when things get complicated,

76
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:21,172
because the truth is...

77
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:25,843
Nero is just using Florence
to get to Antonia.

78
00:07:14,993 --> 00:07:16,361
For you.

79
00:07:16,361 --> 00:07:18,729
Thank you.

80
00:07:19,364 --> 00:07:22,399
You're so sweet. Thank you.

81
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:26,504
Did you like it?

82
00:07:26,504 --> 00:07:28,806
Yes, thank you.

83
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:32,743
Ouch, it hurts.

84
00:07:34,145 --> 00:07:35,980
That's painful.

85
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:38,649
So painful.

86
00:07:39,884 --> 00:07:43,454
So imagine what Florence is feeling...

87
00:07:44,222 --> 00:07:48,326
based on her disposition and her cooking.

88
00:07:48,326 --> 00:07:51,563
Good luck with our food
for the next few weeks.

89
00:07:51,563 --> 00:07:54,999
Or worse... months!

90
00:08:14,819 --> 00:08:16,788
Ms. Serafica?

91
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,623
Grandfather Garp?

92
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,592
Hey!

93
00:08:20,592 --> 00:08:22,760
I already told you the truth!

94
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:29,512
Nero?

95
00:08:29,512 --> 00:08:31,313
Nero?

96
00:08:32,886 --> 00:08:34,439
Nero?

97
00:08:34,439 --> 00:08:36,307
Nero?

98
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:39,644
Don Ferell, Nero is not here.

99
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:42,847
My goodness, where did that kid go?

100
00:08:42,847 --> 00:08:43,882
Don Ferell...

101
00:08:43,882 --> 00:08:47,151
Don Ferell, I saw Nero.

102
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:09,841
Do you remember the first time we met?

103
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:12,777
And you mistook me for someone else.

104
00:09:12,777 --> 00:09:16,280
You thought I was the one
being set up with you.

105
00:09:16,915 --> 00:09:19,984
But what I didn't understand is,

106
00:09:19,984 --> 00:09:24,421
why do you assume that I would agree
to go on a blind date with you?

107
00:09:26,736 --> 00:09:30,072
I was just thinking
if my grandfather would set me up,

108
00:09:30,762 --> 00:09:33,364
it would be with someone worth my time.

109
00:09:34,321 --> 00:09:36,122
Am I?

110
00:09:37,431 --> 00:09:39,565
Am I worth your time?

111
00:09:43,563 --> 00:09:46,899
I will always treasure the time
that I spent with you.

112
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:51,660
How about her?

113
00:09:52,873 --> 00:09:55,074
Is she worth your time?

114
00:10:00,325 --> 00:10:03,527
What I know is,
I'm happy when I'm with her.

115
00:10:05,035 --> 00:10:08,371
Did you tell her about your true feelings?

116
00:10:11,993 --> 00:10:14,461
What are you waiting for?

117
00:10:18,903 --> 00:10:20,838
I'm scared.

118
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:24,988
You're right to be afraid.

119
00:10:25,634 --> 00:10:31,995
Florence is ambitious,
and you are her way out of poverty.

120
00:10:31,995 --> 00:10:35,764
Basically, her entry ticket to our world.

121
00:10:36,718 --> 00:10:38,952
Do you think that she loves you?

122
00:10:40,518 --> 00:10:42,987
Florence is not that kind of person.

123
00:10:42,987 --> 00:10:44,322
All right.

124
00:10:44,322 --> 00:10:46,758
Let's say, you're correct.

125
00:10:46,758 --> 00:10:49,293
Do you think that she loves you?

126
00:10:50,261 --> 00:10:52,496
What if she hurts you?

127
00:10:53,197 --> 00:10:55,899
Do you think you can still recover?

128
00:10:57,035 --> 00:11:00,071
I'm the only one who truly loves you, Nero.

129
00:11:00,071 --> 00:11:02,540
I'm the only one who can understand you.

130
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:06,377
I will always protect you
and I'll never break your heart.

131
00:11:07,011 --> 00:11:09,247
What are you talking about?

132
00:11:09,247 --> 00:11:11,282
Break up with her.

133
00:11:11,282 --> 00:11:15,786
Finish whatever it is you have,
and let's get back together.

134
00:11:16,721 --> 00:11:18,723
Do you think I still want
to reconcile with you?

135
00:11:18,723 --> 00:11:21,392
Do you think you have a choice, Nero?

136
00:11:24,762 --> 00:11:27,031
I can destroy her.

137
00:11:27,031 --> 00:11:31,069
She lied in front of the school
when she agreed to be your girlfriend.

138
00:11:31,069 --> 00:11:32,804
And I can make a case to the dean

139
00:11:32,804 --> 00:11:37,541
that it's a violation of
the ethical standards of our school.

140
00:11:39,744 --> 00:11:42,146
And the least that could happen is...

141
00:11:42,146 --> 00:11:44,849
it could warrant a suspension.

142
00:11:44,849 --> 00:11:46,851
And if I'm not mistaken,

143
00:11:46,851 --> 00:11:49,921
that suspension could cancel her scholarship.

144
00:11:49,921 --> 00:11:53,057
Grandfather Garp won't allow that.

145
00:11:53,057 --> 00:11:56,427
The Ferell Family
isn't the only influential one.

146
00:11:56,427 --> 00:11:59,464
My family is pretty capable too.

147
00:11:59,464 --> 00:12:03,101
But if you hurt his only daughter,

148
00:12:03,101 --> 00:12:07,805
maybe he'll start looking
in a different direction.

149
00:12:07,805 --> 00:12:12,209
Maybe even towards the direction
of the Almeros.

150
00:12:13,177 --> 00:12:16,147
If you don't get back with me,

151
00:12:16,147 --> 00:12:17,849
I will make sure

152
00:12:17,849 --> 00:12:21,285
that Florence will not just
be kicked out of university.

153
00:12:21,285 --> 00:12:29,127
But also, none of her dreams and ambitions
will come true.

154
00:12:29,127 --> 00:12:34,699
And I'll make sure that she'll end up
in the slums where she came from,

155
00:12:34,699 --> 00:12:37,368
and she can be selling lunches
in plastic containers

156
00:12:37,368 --> 00:12:40,037
at construction sites.

157
00:12:40,705 --> 00:12:43,341
I did my research on her.

158
00:12:43,341 --> 00:12:46,177
Do you know the condition of her father?

159
00:12:46,177 --> 00:12:49,147
Florence is an easy target.

160
00:12:49,147 --> 00:12:53,917
And I can hurt her in ways
that you can't even imagine.

161
00:13:09,167 --> 00:13:11,235
She's my girlfriend.

162
00:13:28,119 --> 00:13:32,022
Shall we, my Chummy pie?

163
00:13:50,408 --> 00:13:53,076
Take a look, is it beautiful?

164
00:14:00,852 --> 00:14:02,953
It's really beautiful.

165
00:14:05,102 --> 00:14:06,903
You're right...

166
00:14:07,625 --> 00:14:10,027
it's so beautiful.

167
00:14:11,829 --> 00:14:14,431
Okay, you can use the other side.

168
00:14:33,284 --> 00:14:35,085
Nero!

169
00:14:37,355 --> 00:14:39,891
I've been calling and calling.

170
00:14:39,891 --> 00:14:42,393
You had us all worried.

171
00:14:42,393 --> 00:14:44,428
I'm sorry, Grandfather.

172
00:15:02,825 --> 00:15:04,760
Go ahead and rest.

173
00:15:09,353 --> 00:15:10,954
It's okay.

174
00:15:23,301 --> 00:15:25,402
- I just want to...
- Hey, stop.

175
00:15:26,070 --> 00:15:28,438
I know what you're going to say.

176
00:15:29,707 --> 00:15:33,177
And... what I can only say is,

177
00:15:33,177 --> 00:15:35,947
we don't have to talk about that anymore.

178
00:15:35,947 --> 00:15:39,050
Our agreement was clear.

179
00:15:39,050 --> 00:15:40,884
So...

180
00:15:41,586 --> 00:15:46,958
I have no right to feel bad.

181
00:15:46,958 --> 00:15:50,461
I should be happy, right?

182
00:15:50,461 --> 00:15:55,032
Because it seems like you and Antonia
are now okay.

183
00:15:55,032 --> 00:15:57,335
It's mission accomplished.

184
00:15:57,335 --> 00:16:01,638
We succeeded in making her jealous.

185
00:16:06,777 --> 00:16:08,522
Yes.

186
00:16:11,315 --> 00:16:13,784
It's good that you understand.

187
00:16:15,853 --> 00:16:19,956
But still... thanks for your help.

188
00:16:21,993 --> 00:16:24,259
I am now happy knowing you'll be able

189
00:16:24,259 --> 00:16:26,532
to achieve your dreams for yourself...

190
00:16:26,532 --> 00:16:28,699
and your family.

191
00:16:36,674 --> 00:16:39,009
You didn't assume, right?

192
00:16:43,414 --> 00:16:44,919
No.

193
00:16:45,950 --> 00:16:47,473
Good.

194
00:16:48,219 --> 00:16:51,254
I really wish you
all the happiness you deserve.

195
00:16:52,423 --> 00:16:54,658
Good luck, Florence.

196
00:17:08,873 --> 00:17:11,059
<i>I am now happy knowing you'll be able</i>

197
00:17:11,059 --> 00:17:13,403
<i>to achieve your dreams for yourself...</i>

198
00:17:13,403 --> 00:17:15,947
<i>and your family.</i>

199
00:17:15,947 --> 00:17:19,254
"I am now happy knowing you'll be able

200
00:17:19,254 --> 00:17:21,686
to achieve your dreams

201
00:17:21,686 --> 00:17:25,322
for yourself and your family"?

202
00:17:26,457 --> 00:17:28,392
What?

203
00:17:28,392 --> 00:17:31,429
What did he mean by that?

204
00:17:31,429 --> 00:17:34,898
I won't be able to achieve my dreams before?

205
00:17:38,636 --> 00:17:40,165
Hey!

206
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:44,909
So, are you okay now?

207
00:17:44,909 --> 00:17:46,477
What kind of question is that?

208
00:17:46,477 --> 00:17:48,445
Of course not.

209
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:52,249
Florence is not defined by men.

210
00:17:52,249 --> 00:17:54,751
I'm sure she's okay now.

211
00:17:56,087 --> 00:17:57,388
Why did you bother to ask me

212
00:17:57,388 --> 00:18:01,726
if you have your own opinions
whether I'm okay or not?

213
00:18:01,726 --> 00:18:03,994
So, what's the answer?

214
00:18:08,766 --> 00:18:12,607
I'm okay but I'm somehow...

215
00:18:12,607 --> 00:18:15,492
still annoyed with what happened,

216
00:18:15,492 --> 00:18:20,444
but what can I do
when I'm just a simple Dela Cruz, right?

217
00:18:20,444 --> 00:18:27,217
And I went to GU to study
and achieve my dreams.

218
00:18:29,053 --> 00:18:31,522
So...

219
00:18:31,522 --> 00:18:33,924
what's your plan?

220
00:18:33,924 --> 00:18:36,160
Plan on what?

221
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,362
On how to invade a country?

222
00:18:38,362 --> 00:18:42,032
Of course, what are your plans for the ball?

223
00:18:43,401 --> 00:18:45,069
Nothing.

224
00:18:45,069 --> 00:18:47,071
What do you mean by nothing?

225
00:18:47,071 --> 00:18:49,673
Nothing. As in, nothing.

226
00:18:49,673 --> 00:18:52,476
- Nothing?
- I already told you.

227
00:18:52,476 --> 00:18:56,781
I don't have 50,000 pesos
for that per-plate meal.

228
00:18:56,781 --> 00:18:59,450
And since I don't have a date anymore,

229
00:18:59,450 --> 00:19:02,186
and I don't have money for that,

230
00:19:02,186 --> 00:19:05,856
do I really have to fight for that ball?

231
00:19:05,856 --> 00:19:09,693
You know what?
Sometimes I hate poor people.

232
00:19:09,693 --> 00:19:13,330
You act like you don't have
rich kid friends in us.

233
00:19:13,330 --> 00:19:14,432
That's right.

234
00:19:14,432 --> 00:19:17,568
Plus, the best revenge is to be beautiful.

235
00:19:17,568 --> 00:19:19,070
And the best place to be beautiful

236
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:21,872
is at the Grand Gyronella University Ball.

237
00:19:21,872 --> 00:19:23,974
Exactly.

238
00:19:23,974 --> 00:19:27,344
Except for the judgment of poor people,

239
00:19:27,344 --> 00:19:29,513
I agree with Camille and Aira.

240
00:19:29,513 --> 00:19:32,383
We can contribute to cover for you.

241
00:19:32,383 --> 00:19:35,553
That will go to a good cause, right?

242
00:19:35,553 --> 00:19:38,055
And we're excited about a makeover.

243
00:19:38,055 --> 00:19:40,357
Yes!

244
00:19:40,357 --> 00:19:41,826
Makeover?

245
00:19:41,826 --> 00:19:43,247
Yes.

246
00:19:44,161 --> 00:19:46,297
- Me?
- Yes.

247
00:19:46,297 --> 00:19:48,132
Makeover.

248
00:19:48,132 --> 00:19:49,433
I don't want to.

249
00:19:49,433 --> 00:19:51,669
Don't experiment on me.

250
00:19:51,669 --> 00:19:54,138
But you're our friend, Florence.

251
00:19:54,138 --> 00:19:56,273
Friends help each other.

252
00:19:56,273 --> 00:19:59,410
Friends are always there for each other.

253
00:19:59,410 --> 00:20:02,913
And friends party together!

254
00:20:02,913 --> 00:20:05,649
Friends always offer a helping hand.

255
00:20:05,649 --> 00:20:08,252
And when you get murdered,

256
00:20:08,252 --> 00:20:11,655
we, your friends, will avenge your death.

257
00:20:11,655 --> 00:20:13,490
True.

258
00:20:14,191 --> 00:20:16,760
You're overreacting with the murder part.

259
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,763
So, game?

260
00:21:02,396 --> 00:21:03,922
No.

261
00:21:05,476 --> 00:21:06,969
Look.

262
00:21:18,889 --> 00:21:23,060
Yes... I think we found it.

263
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:24,428
Perfection.

264
00:21:24,428 --> 00:21:26,896
I agree.

265
00:21:43,734 --> 00:21:48,352
[Follow The Flowers]

266
00:21:48,352 --> 00:21:49,853
What's this?

267
00:21:49,853 --> 00:21:52,067
Follow the flowers?

268
00:21:52,067 --> 00:21:55,291
There are flowers and candles.

269
00:22:08,467 --> 00:22:11,434
[Watch Your Step]

270
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,667
[Watch Your Step]

271
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,434
[Will You Be My Date?]

272
00:23:27,518 --> 00:23:28,919
I'm just making you laugh.

273
00:23:28,919 --> 00:23:34,458
But it doesn't change the fact
that my scrambled eggs are delicious.

274
00:23:34,458 --> 00:23:38,429
Tomorrow, I'll have sunny side up.

275
00:23:38,429 --> 00:23:41,031
So, you like eggs.

276
00:23:41,031 --> 00:23:44,033
Take it easy, you might turn into a chicken.

277
00:23:45,112 --> 00:23:46,597
Good one.

278
00:23:47,636 --> 00:23:50,800
So just cry it all out.

279
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:54,344
Take out all the pain
you're feeling right now.

280
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,656
To be fair...

281
00:24:05,656 --> 00:24:11,961
you said words that made me feel better now.

282
00:24:18,769 --> 00:24:20,703
Florence...

283
00:24:21,405 --> 00:24:23,339
What happened?

284
00:24:47,765 --> 00:24:50,900
So... will you be my date?

285
00:24:54,304 --> 00:24:56,906
Don't you have any other choice?

286
00:25:32,376 --> 00:25:33,877
Ma'am Serafica?

287
00:25:33,877 --> 00:25:35,212
Am I late already?

288
00:25:35,212 --> 00:25:36,480
I will cook right away.

289
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:38,849
No, you will not cook today.

290
00:25:38,849 --> 00:25:40,484
I will take care of the house.

291
00:25:40,484 --> 00:25:42,319
You focus on the ball.

292
00:25:42,319 --> 00:25:45,355
I believe this is
a very important day, right?

293
00:25:45,355 --> 00:25:46,590
No, Ma'am Serafica.

294
00:25:46,590 --> 00:25:49,593
- That will be easy and...
- I don't think so.

295
00:25:49,593 --> 00:25:51,829
Because someone informed me

296
00:25:51,829 --> 00:25:54,965
that you'll be needing at least one whole day
to prepare.

297
00:25:54,965 --> 00:25:56,266
- What?
- Yes.

298
00:25:56,266 --> 00:25:58,534
Who said that?

299
00:26:05,342 --> 00:26:07,277
Ma'am Serafica, what is going on?

300
00:26:07,277 --> 00:26:10,680
And who said that I have to
prepare the whole day?

301
00:26:24,461 --> 00:26:26,242
Them?

302
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:29,933
What are you doing here?

303
00:26:29,933 --> 00:26:34,872
Girl, we weren't informed
that you're staying here in the mansion.

304
00:26:34,872 --> 00:26:39,443
I heard you're a scholar of Don Ferell,
but to actually live here?

305
00:26:39,443 --> 00:26:43,247
So, is it always a fun time
with the Ferell boys?

306
00:26:43,247 --> 00:26:44,515
Will you stop it?

307
00:26:44,515 --> 00:26:46,950
I'm a cook here.

308
00:26:46,950 --> 00:26:49,419
So what do you cook for the Ferells?

309
00:26:49,419 --> 00:26:51,421
And as the saying goes,

310
00:26:51,421 --> 00:26:54,291
have you made your way to their hearts?

311
00:26:54,291 --> 00:26:58,562
Will you tell me why you're here?
Or I'll throw you out.

312
00:26:58,562 --> 00:27:00,964
Hey, you easily get mad.

313
00:27:00,964 --> 00:27:06,069
Well, we brought you your glam team.

314
00:27:06,069 --> 00:27:08,204
Glam team?

315
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:11,100
Why?

316
00:27:11,100 --> 00:27:14,610
Do you think
you're going to the ball unprepared?

317
00:27:15,279 --> 00:27:16,580
What?

318
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:18,681
There they are.

319
00:27:21,218 --> 00:27:23,553
What do you mean?

320
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:30,261
This is it, guys.

321
00:27:30,261 --> 00:27:32,963
Welcome to this year's Grand Gyronella Ball.

322
00:27:32,963 --> 00:27:35,833
A celebration of humanity and beauty.

323
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:41,245
And in a world full of people who are angry
and want to hurt others...

324
00:27:41,245 --> 00:27:44,274
this year's theme will be
"Return to Kindness".

325
00:27:44,274 --> 00:27:49,346
We are here live at Levante Continental
for the Grand Gyronella ball.

326
00:27:49,346 --> 00:27:52,649
But this year,
there's a difference in our celebration

327
00:27:52,649 --> 00:27:56,233
because it's not just glitz and glamour.

328
00:27:56,233 --> 00:27:59,236
This is also a celebration of humanity.

329
00:27:59,236 --> 00:28:01,538
In fact, for the very first time...

330
00:28:01,538 --> 00:28:04,875
Oh, look at who we have here.

331
00:28:04,875 --> 00:28:10,514
Linalyn Ysabel Tibayan Hidalgo,
more commonly known as Lina,

332
00:28:10,514 --> 00:28:13,417
she literally is the luckiest girl
on the campus

333
00:28:13,417 --> 00:28:17,988
because she is literally lucky
coming from a family who won the lottery.

334
00:28:17,988 --> 00:28:20,122
What I can only say is...

335
00:28:21,158 --> 00:28:23,860
I hope it's for everyone.

336
00:28:25,062 --> 00:28:27,630
She looks so beautiful.

337
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,535
A lot of the students here in Gyronella

338
00:28:31,535 --> 00:28:33,804
look like they're wearing gowns
from different designers,

339
00:28:33,804 --> 00:28:36,606
may it be from the Philippines
or all over the world.

340
00:28:36,606 --> 00:28:39,775
I cannot wait to see
what everyone else is wearing.

341
00:28:44,147 --> 00:28:47,951
Oh, who would have thought
these two will recover

342
00:28:47,951 --> 00:28:50,320
from the debacle that is Agora day.

343
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:55,192
We have Camille Villarico Cortez
and Aira Samson Rivera,

344
00:28:55,192 --> 00:28:58,562
the famous "Take it-Take it"
of the Gyronella University.

345
00:28:58,562 --> 00:29:02,832
Because if you take the other,
you automatically get the other one.

346
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:06,069
It's so beautiful here at the Grand GU Ball

347
00:29:06,069 --> 00:29:08,004
and I love our theme for this year.

348
00:29:08,004 --> 00:29:10,474
It's super groundbreaking

349
00:29:10,474 --> 00:29:12,743
because this year's theme
is all about serving people,

350
00:29:12,743 --> 00:29:17,780
those who can't reach,
like, the ones in our university.

351
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:25,789
Oh my goodness!

352
00:29:25,789 --> 00:29:29,159
Looks like the Ferell Brothers
won't be arriving in five today.

353
00:29:29,159 --> 00:29:33,230
Well, it's about time they stop
acting like a boy band group.

354
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:37,934
In fact, I have a very interesting trivia
about the Ferell brothers.

355
00:29:37,934 --> 00:29:43,240
Because the term Ferell Brothers
is actually a misnomer

356
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:47,377
because they are not brothers,
but first cousins.

357
00:29:47,377 --> 00:29:52,849
And I think this is a testament
to how well Don Ferell raised them

358
00:29:52,849 --> 00:29:55,285
because even if they are not brothers,

359
00:29:55,285 --> 00:29:59,855
they grew up in a tight-knit family
despite being insanely wealthy.

360
00:30:14,738 --> 00:30:18,475
Oh, and speaking of Don Ferell,

361
00:30:18,475 --> 00:30:21,645
it truly is an honor
to be graced by his presence.

362
00:30:21,645 --> 00:30:24,247
Because if there's a person
who is referred to in the saying,

363
00:30:24,247 --> 00:30:28,885
"need no further introduction",
it's probably him.

364
00:30:28,885 --> 00:30:32,222
Because what else can I say about him

365
00:30:32,222 --> 00:30:35,225
that hasn't been said yet
in his numerous features

366
00:30:35,225 --> 00:30:38,328
and various business magazines?

367
00:30:38,328 --> 00:30:41,631
Thank you so much for attending tonight,
Don Ferell.

368
00:30:54,010 --> 00:30:55,412
All of the people here in Gyronella

369
00:30:55,412 --> 00:30:57,681
are actually so excited for this year's theme

370
00:30:57,681 --> 00:31:00,116
because it's groundbreaking.

371
00:31:00,116 --> 00:31:05,454
I mean, we're so used
to just glitz and glamour, and partying...

372
00:31:06,456 --> 00:31:10,193
Oh, this is a surprise.

373
00:31:10,193 --> 00:31:11,533
So surprising

374
00:31:11,534 --> 00:31:14,364
that I didn't prepare an introduction
for him.

375
00:31:14,364 --> 00:31:17,133
But who needs cue cards or whatnot,

376
00:31:17,133 --> 00:31:21,171
if you're Don Rogelio Almero
of the Almero Group of Companies?

377
00:31:21,171 --> 00:31:23,840
So, the rumors must be true then,

378
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:27,310
that the Almeros have taken an interest
in our beloved university.

379
00:31:27,310 --> 00:31:29,224
The Dean must be really excited,

380
00:31:29,224 --> 00:31:33,383
because the entrance of Almeros
to our beloved university

381
00:31:33,383 --> 00:31:37,186
would mean
a very significant financial contribution.

382
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:56,373
Ma'am Serafica, how is Florence?
We're already late.

383
00:31:56,373 --> 00:31:57,774
Bad news, Owen.

384
00:31:57,774 --> 00:32:00,143
It looks like
Florence doesn't want to go anymore.

385
00:32:00,143 --> 00:32:03,280
She's been locking herself in the room
for quite some time now.

386
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:05,381
What happened?

387
00:32:09,352 --> 00:32:14,891
And it looks like the king and queen
have arrived.

388
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:20,730
Here we have
Ms. Antonia Scarlet Vamorida Fuentes,

389
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:25,768
escorted by none other
than Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell.

390
00:32:43,353 --> 00:32:47,490
Antonia looks perfect in her sparkly,

391
00:32:47,490 --> 00:32:49,559
like-a-night-filled-with-stars dress.

392
00:32:49,559 --> 00:32:52,895
I think that's how I would be describing it.

393
00:33:08,378 --> 00:33:11,715
Girls... where's our chicken?

394
00:33:11,715 --> 00:33:14,951
I don't think there's a chicken
on our menu for tonight, Camille.

395
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:16,252
Lina.

396
00:33:16,252 --> 00:33:19,322
What she meant was,
where is the person we're rooting for?

397
00:33:19,322 --> 00:33:21,458
Where is Florence?

398
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:23,282
Exactly.

399
00:33:24,527 --> 00:33:26,363
Oh my gosh.

400
00:33:26,363 --> 00:33:28,571
Where is she?

401
00:33:32,068 --> 00:33:33,803
Florence?

402
00:33:33,803 --> 00:33:35,505
Can we just talk?

403
00:33:35,505 --> 00:33:36,806
No need.

404
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:38,641
I don't want people to see me, Owen.

405
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:40,343
I look like a fool.

406
00:33:40,343 --> 00:33:42,379
Come on, Florence, it can't be that bad.

407
00:33:42,379 --> 00:33:44,614
Please, Owen, this is not me.

408
00:33:44,614 --> 00:33:47,650
You'll all laugh at me once you see me.

409
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:49,486
I just want to see you and who knows,

410
00:33:49,486 --> 00:33:52,288
maybe Ma'am Serafica and I can help you.

411
00:33:56,459 --> 00:33:59,295
Ma'am, here are the keys. I'm sorry.

412
00:33:59,295 --> 00:34:01,698
Please step aside. I will now open the door.

413
00:34:01,698 --> 00:34:04,700
- Okay.
- So we'll find out what's wrong.

414
00:34:20,550 --> 00:34:23,152
Okay, thank you for the update.

415
00:34:24,754 --> 00:34:26,300
What's going on?

416
00:34:26,300 --> 00:34:28,613
Is Florence okay?

417
00:34:28,613 --> 00:34:31,961
It seems she's not happy
with how she turned out earlier,

418
00:34:31,961 --> 00:34:35,432
that's why the stylist said
that she might not come.

419
00:34:35,432 --> 00:34:36,933
What?

420
00:34:36,933 --> 00:34:40,170
It can't be that bad.

421
00:34:40,170 --> 00:34:45,474
I want to get out of here and go to her
to really see what's happening.

422
00:34:48,311 --> 00:34:49,779
She can't do this.

423
00:34:49,779 --> 00:34:52,214
She has to be here.

424
00:34:56,086 --> 00:34:57,420
Florence is here.

425
00:34:57,420 --> 00:34:59,288
What?

426
00:35:01,524 --> 00:35:03,566
Wow!

427
00:35:03,566 --> 00:35:06,835
That is crazy, bro!

428
00:35:08,731 --> 00:35:12,902
I'm not going to lie. They look good.

429
00:35:38,361 --> 00:35:40,930
- Florence is so beautiful.
- Right.

430
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:44,100
And she looks so rich in what she's wearing.

431
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:46,063
I agree.

432
00:35:46,063 --> 00:35:50,233
Didn't I tell you?
Everything will be all right.

433
00:35:50,987 --> 00:35:53,055
You look perfect.

434
00:36:05,788 --> 00:36:06,956
Go, Florence.

435
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:10,860
Raise the flag of people like us
at the poverty level.

436
00:36:10,860 --> 00:36:15,056
Babycakes, just let it be.

437
00:36:15,056 --> 00:36:20,801
Our point is,
to let Florence carry out our dream.

438
00:36:20,801 --> 00:36:21,354
Well...

439
00:36:21,355 --> 00:36:25,508
What's important is
for all of us to be happy and...

440
00:36:25,508 --> 00:36:29,399
Celebrate!

441
00:36:29,400 --> 00:36:30,900
Oh my gosh.

442
00:36:30,901 --> 00:36:34,250
To be fair, girl,
you're one of the contenders.

443
00:36:34,250 --> 00:36:36,845
You're part of the top five here.

444
00:36:36,845 --> 00:36:40,306
Also, she has the best accessory.

445
00:36:40,306 --> 00:36:42,725
What accessory?

446
00:36:42,725 --> 00:36:46,240
What else, but... a Ferell.

447
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:48,965
Ferell.

448
00:36:48,965 --> 00:36:52,001
I'm just happy to be here
and spend time with you girls.

449
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:54,771
Really, and you're trying to be cute, Owen.

450
00:36:54,771 --> 00:36:57,974
You're the topnotcher of the Ferells.

451
00:36:57,974 --> 00:37:00,677
Which brings me to my point.

452
00:37:00,677 --> 00:37:03,045
Look at the other Ferells...

453
00:37:04,801 --> 00:37:09,281
It looks like our fundraising for tonight
will be lucrative.

454
00:37:09,281 --> 00:37:11,353
Exactly.

455
00:37:12,531 --> 00:37:14,531
Good thing your friend gave us a side hustle.

456
00:37:14,531 --> 00:37:17,273
Yes, we can have extra funds
for our household budget.

457
00:37:17,273 --> 00:37:18,968
What kind of event is this?

458
00:37:18,968 --> 00:37:20,729
I'm wondering too.

459
00:37:21,788 --> 00:37:23,399
This is the Gyronella University event.

460
00:37:23,399 --> 00:37:26,234
Yes, you're right.

461
00:37:26,234 --> 00:37:27,824
Maybe your daughter is there.

462
00:37:27,824 --> 00:37:28,905
No, I don't think so.

463
00:37:28,905 --> 00:37:31,163
They said it's 50,000 pesos per plate here.

464
00:37:31,163 --> 00:37:34,431
Where are we going to get the money
to pay for that?

465
00:37:34,431 --> 00:37:36,646
- Let's call her.
- Okay, go ahead and call her.

466
00:37:36,646 --> 00:37:38,585
Let me fish out my phone.

467
00:37:40,550 --> 00:37:42,285
Hello.

468
00:37:42,285 --> 00:37:43,786
Florence?

469
00:37:43,786 --> 00:37:45,555
Oh, I'm so sorry.

470
00:37:45,555 --> 00:37:47,690
This is Serafica.

471
00:37:47,690 --> 00:37:52,227
Florence left her cellphone behind.

472
00:37:52,829 --> 00:37:54,297
Where is she?

473
00:37:54,297 --> 00:37:56,099
She didn't tell you?

474
00:37:56,099 --> 00:37:57,649
What?

475
00:37:59,102 --> 00:38:01,170
The reason why she's not here

476
00:38:01,170 --> 00:38:05,008
is that she's attending the Grand GU Ball.

477
00:38:05,008 --> 00:38:07,977
But don't worry because once you see her,

478
00:38:07,977 --> 00:38:12,348
I'm sure you'll both be
very proud of her, okay?

479
00:38:12,348 --> 00:38:13,950
Bye.

480
00:38:13,950 --> 00:38:15,784
Come on.

481
00:38:20,010 --> 00:38:21,508
Babycakes?

482
00:38:21,508 --> 00:38:23,426
Isn't that just a code?

483
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:27,530
Hey, Buttercup, you got jealous right away.

484
00:38:27,530 --> 00:38:29,799
Maybe that's someone else.

485
00:38:29,799 --> 00:38:31,534
What do you mean it's someone else?

486
00:38:31,534 --> 00:38:34,704
Enough, my goodness gracious.

487
00:38:34,704 --> 00:38:35,972
- Stop it.
- I'm the only one you love?

488
00:38:35,972 --> 00:38:40,243
Of course, my Babycup.

489
00:38:40,243 --> 00:38:41,878
I love it when I do this.

490
00:38:41,878 --> 00:38:43,413
I just love it.

491
00:38:43,413 --> 00:38:44,614
I'm the only one she loves.

492
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:46,683
Of course.

493
00:38:46,683 --> 00:38:49,419
- Really. Cheers!
- Cheers!

494
00:38:49,419 --> 00:38:53,456
- Salute!
- Salute!

495
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:59,495
Don Ferell, I don't think I need
to introduce you to Don Rogelio.

496
00:39:00,430 --> 00:39:03,398
Please call me Rogelio, Dean.

497
00:39:04,086 --> 00:39:07,106
I just want to say, Mr. Rogelio,

498
00:39:07,106 --> 00:39:11,174
that we thank you with all our hearts
for your donation.

499
00:39:11,174 --> 00:39:13,910
And with the support of the Ferells,

500
00:39:13,910 --> 00:39:17,869
our university can expand
the scholarship program

501
00:39:17,869 --> 00:39:22,985
so we can accommodate
more students who are not as fortunate,

502
00:39:22,985 --> 00:39:28,124
but deserving of the quality of education
the school gives.

503
00:39:28,124 --> 00:39:29,292
Thank you, Rogelio.

504
00:39:29,292 --> 00:39:32,095
Thank you for your generosity.

505
00:39:32,095 --> 00:39:34,263
You're welcome, Garpidio.

506
00:39:34,997 --> 00:39:38,158
It's about time that we work together
to create a positive impact

507
00:39:38,158 --> 00:39:40,737
on the lives of the majority.

508
00:39:40,737 --> 00:39:42,538
I agree.

509
00:39:59,672 --> 00:40:02,641
She looks like someone familiar, right?

510
00:40:05,495 --> 00:40:08,000
I don't know what you're talking about.

511
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,665
I think it's the eyes.

512
00:40:09,665 --> 00:40:12,702
That's what I also noticed
the first time I saw her.

513
00:40:12,702 --> 00:40:16,238
It kind of looks like Alyanna.

514
00:40:18,203 --> 00:40:21,398
Are you suggesting
that she's the missing daughter of Alyanna?

515
00:40:33,122 --> 00:40:36,467
The biggest party on this side of the world
is about to start.

516
00:40:36,467 --> 00:40:39,236
Are you ready
for the super spreader event of the season?

517
00:40:39,236 --> 00:40:44,742
Because we will be spreading
both fun and goodwill at the same time.

518
00:40:44,742 --> 00:40:46,077
So, what are you waiting for?

519
00:40:46,077 --> 00:40:49,679
Return to party,
Return to Kindness starts now.

520
00:40:51,449 --> 00:40:53,651
Fundraising?

521
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:57,588
Well, Florence, since you left me in charge,

522
00:40:57,588 --> 00:41:03,194
we thought of different activities
to raise funds for the poor.

523
00:41:03,194 --> 00:41:04,462
Trust me, Florence,

524
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:08,132
even I was impressed with
the idea of Camille and Aira.

525
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:10,334
Yes.

526
00:41:10,334 --> 00:41:14,371
I'm excited about whatever activity is that.

527
00:41:18,242 --> 00:41:20,544
Powerful.

528
00:41:21,712 --> 00:41:23,247
Let's go.

529
00:41:23,247 --> 00:41:26,217
Hey, now you know.

530
00:41:26,217 --> 00:41:28,685
You learned how to do it, Lina.

531
00:41:36,093 --> 00:41:37,928
Stop that.

532
00:41:37,928 --> 00:41:39,763
Stop looking at her.

533
00:41:43,097 --> 00:41:48,272
At least now you know
what type of a woman Florence is.

534
00:41:48,272 --> 00:41:50,941
Or maybe you should continue looking at her.

535
00:41:53,043 --> 00:41:57,415
Imagine, she's now with Owen.

536
00:41:57,415 --> 00:42:00,718
She easily moved on from you.

537
00:42:00,718 --> 00:42:03,486
And that just raises my suspicion of her.

538
00:42:06,857 --> 00:42:11,928
She was just using you to level up her life.

539
00:42:14,565 --> 00:42:18,229
And because you're no longer an option,

540
00:42:18,229 --> 00:42:21,305
she quickly looked for an alternative.

541
00:42:21,305 --> 00:42:23,707
She soon looked for someone else.

542
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:37,521
Excuse me.

543
00:42:37,521 --> 00:42:39,589
One more, please.

544
00:42:47,698 --> 00:42:52,636
So now, may we call on for the next item,
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz?

545
00:42:52,636 --> 00:42:56,100
For this item, Florence will be
cooking you a private dinner

546
00:42:56,100 --> 00:42:58,069
and a set-up by the beach.

547
00:42:58,069 --> 00:43:00,309
So, Ms. Florence?

548
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:04,715
Let's get this bidding started.

549
00:43:04,715 --> 00:43:08,018
Private dinner cooked by Ms. Florence.

550
00:43:08,018 --> 00:43:09,853
Anyone?

551
00:43:10,515 --> 00:43:12,550
One million pesos.

552
00:43:15,926 --> 00:43:19,597
It's you who said that Florence is our cook,

553
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:22,900
and it's not good to see
that both Ferells are fighting because of her.

554
00:43:22,900 --> 00:43:25,402
Sit together and talk.

555
00:43:25,402 --> 00:43:26,604
Man-to-man.

556
00:43:26,604 --> 00:43:28,056
A Ferell to a Ferell.

557
00:43:28,056 --> 00:43:30,541
I don't care what others will say.

558
00:43:30,541 --> 00:43:33,310
My God, dude, you're both Ferells.

559
00:43:33,310 --> 00:43:35,646
Have you forgotten what Grandpa said?

560
00:43:35,646 --> 00:43:40,811
That if Ferells have a problem,
we fix it together.

561
00:43:40,811 --> 00:43:43,687
That's right. You better fix your problem.

562
00:43:43,687 --> 00:43:46,290
The last thing we want
is to tear each other apart

563
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:48,425
because of Florence.

564
00:43:52,246 --> 00:43:55,866
Florence, what happened?

565
00:43:55,866 --> 00:43:57,734
Is there a problem?
